.TH ED 1
.SH NAME
ed \- line editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ed
.RB [ -o " | " -
.RI | file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ed
is the classic line-oriented text editor: it reads commands from
standard input describing lines or ranges of the file being edited
and what to do with them (print, change, delete, substitute with a
regular expression, and so on), one command per line, rather than
presenting a screen-editing view.
.PP
.I File
is loaded initially if given.
.B -
suppresses the usual byte-count messages (the classic
.B ed
"silent" convention).
.B -o
starts with an empty buffer and directs the final write to standard
output rather than a named file, for use as a filter driven entirely
by editing commands read from standard input.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/ed.b
